{
  "$comment": "Golden vectors for the photo pick, photo/{head_id}/pick (sync.proto rule 6 PHOTO PICK). Every implementation (this package, fc-coordinator's Push validation, fc-mobile) must agree with every case. `pushes`: one pushed SyncEvent each, on `key`. `op` is the SyncOp; the payload on the wire is JSON.stringify(`body`), or `raw` exactly as written when the case has one. `expect` is \"accepted\" or \"payload_invalid\", and `why` says which check refuses: \"schema\" (schemas/photo-pick.schema.json does not validate the payload, or it is not JSON) or \"delete_payload\" (a DELETE carries a payload). A DELETE with an empty payload is accepted and means \"use the default\". `shown`: what a client shows for a figure. `pick` is the derivative_id of the live pick, or null when there is none (never made, or deleted); `images` is the derivative_ids of the figure's GetProductImages list as this viewer is sent it, in order; `expect` is the id shown as the pick: the pick's when `images` carries it, else null, and null reads exactly as no pick (the default is shown, the facet is kept). `lastWriterWins`: the events of one user on one figure's pick; a reader applies an event iff its version is greater than the one it holds (compareVersion), so in EVERY arrival order, repeats included, the pick ends as `expect`: the derivative_id, or null for the default. `merged`: one card after an ER merge (sync.proto ER MERGES). `card` is its head_id and the head ids of its requested_as; `events` is the one event the reader holds on each pick key, live or tombstoned, picks on figures outside the card included; `images` is the merged figure's list. Among the events of card.head_id and every requested_as head, the greatest version decides, the lower head_id (bytewise) between equal versions; `expect.shown` is the decider's id when it is a live pick the list carries, else null (a tombstone, a pick the list lacks, or no event; never an older pick in its place); `expect.write_to` is the head whose key a new pick or a \"use default\" is written to: the decider's, or card.head_id when no head of the card holds an event.",
